      "writtenOn": "2024-07-11T18:46:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "apology, I don\u0027t fully understand your suggestion.\n- Are you saying that we should use the same `MslCompilationRequest` as the key for the in-memory cache and the blob cache? And pass it to the DAWN_TRY_LOAD_OR_RUN (with overloads for in-memory cache \u0026 blob cache)?\n- IIRC what we discussed in the chat group was that we should be able to use a smaller key for the in-memory cache:\n\u003e since the ShaderModule is the same and thus the bindings are the same, the only things that actually can impact MSL output given the shader module is identical are:\n - sampleMask\n - pipeline layout\n - attachment state\n - primitive topology\n - entry point\n - constant overrides\n\u003e it\u0027s much cheaper key using just those bits without full key serialization.\n- If we simply pass full `MslCompilationRequest` key to DAWN_TRY_LOAD_OR_RUN and just compute the hash with subset of the key\u0027s bits for the in-memory cache, then I don\u0027t see any difference from what the current patchset is doing.\n\nAlso the things being done in this CL is a bit similar to vulkan backend\u0027s `ConcurrentTransformedShaderModuleCache` where it only needs a subset of `MslCompilationRequest`\u0027s bits.",
      "parentUuid": "820f3350_6ba7888b",
      "revId": "b7fefb7bb66d12f7de53f72f8676df3e9d2ffa03",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
