      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e And, in this struct, we can put things like pointers, etc. because we\u0027re just hashing it and not serializing to disk. So it\u0027s for sure a smaller key and cheaper to compare.\n\nNote that this is technically incorrect and something we need to fix in the Vulkan backend as well. Two equal pointers to a pipeline layout don\u0027t mean that they are equal because the PL could have been freed and a new one created in the same spot. If we want to do something like this, we\u0027ll need to store a cryptographic hash of the PL in the key.",
      "parentUuid": "f7851457_59c921a6",
      "revId": "b7fefb7bb66d12f7de53f72f8676df3e9d2ffa03",
